  "result": "Perfect! All 52 tests pass (14 new tests for the two functions).\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded two functions to `src/invoices.js` for modifying draft invoices:\n\n**addLine(invoice, { sku, qty})** \u2014 Add or update a line in a draft invoice\n- Adds a new line if the SKU doesn't exist\n- Increases qty if the SKU already exists on the invoice\n- Validates qty is a positive integer (QTY_INVALID)\n- Validates SKU exists in catalogue (UNKNOWN_SKU)\n- Requires invoice status to be 'draft' (NOT_DRAFT)\n- Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with enriched line data from catalogue\n- Does not mutate the input invoice\n\n**removeLine(invoice, sku)** \u2014 Remove a line from a draft invoice\n- Removes the line with the specified SKU\n- Returns LINE_NOT_FOUND if SKU not on invoice\n- Returns NO_LINES if it would be the last line (invoices must have \u22651 line)\n- Requires invoice status to be 'draft' (NOT_DRAFT)\n- Returns `ok(newInvoice)`\n- Does not mutate the input invoice\n\n**Error codes added:**\n- NOT_DRAFT: Cannot modify an invoice that is not in draft status.\n- LINE_NOT_FOUND: No line with that SKU on the invoice.\n\n**Test coverage** \u2014 14 new tests covering:\n- Adding new lines and updating existing line quantities\n- Validation of qty and SKU\n- Status checks for draft-only operations\n- Non-mutation of original invoices\n- Preservation of other invoice properties\n- Preventing removal of the last line\n- Complex workflows combining add/remove operations",
